Subject: [PATCH] hw/net/igb: optional TX offload by context descriptor offsets

Add an "x-desc-offload" property (default off). When on, TSE/TXSM
descriptors are handled like the 82576 does: L4 starts at MACLEN + IPLEN,
the TSO header is MACLEN + IPLEN + L4LEN, the IP header at MACLEN gets its
length/ID and a checksum over the IPLEN range, and the L4 checksum is
completed from the seed the driver left in place. Headers outside that
range (e.g. the outer UDP header of a VXLAN frame) are not touched. The
default path offloads the outermost L4 header it parses instead.

Applies to QEMU 8.2.2 (patch -p1).

